        {
          "unit_id": "first_hire",
          "title": "The First Hire",
          "description": "Matices de necesidad y preferencia: needn't have, didn't need to, would rather, had better.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "first_hire_lesson",
              "title": "needn't have, would rather, had better",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The first hire",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "We needn't have advertised, you know. Helen sent us three excellent CVs yesterday."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I know. And I didn't need to pay for that expensive job advert either. Lesson learned."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Who would you rather hire, the illustrator or the junior developer?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I'd rather we hired a designer first. We've got more design work than code."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Fair enough. But we'd better decide soon. Grace wants the full project by May."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Then we'd better not waste any time. Let's interview both tomorrow."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "You needn't come to the interviews if you're busy. I can do them."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I'd rather be there. It's our first hire; it has to feel right."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Should we have asked Priya? She knows half of Bristol."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "She'd have told us to hire someone who cooks, like Ollie."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "We'd better not tell her we've got a coffee machine, or she'll apply herself."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "March. The pilot was a success, and Green Door Design needs its first employee. Lucía and Daniel are reading applications in the office."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "preference_advice",
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"We needn't have advertised.\" Did they advertise?",
                        "options": [
                          "Yes, but it wasn't necessary",
                          "No"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "tag": "past_modals"
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"I'd rather we hired a designer first.\" After would rather + another subject, the verb is in…",
                        "options": [
                          "the past simple",
                          "the present"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"We'd better decide soon.\" 'd better = …",
                        "options": [
                          "had better (advertencia o consejo fuerte)",
                          "would better"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Who sent them three CVs?",
                        "options": [
                          "Helen",
                          "Grace",
                          "Priya"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "tag": ""
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "past_modals",
                    "title": "needn't have, would rather, had better",
                    "explanation": "Para hablar de necesidad, preferencia y consejo:\n- «needn't have» + participio: hicimos algo que no era necesario: «We needn't have advertised.»\n- «didn't need to» + verbo: no era necesario (y normalmente no lo hicimos): «We didn't need to advertise, so we didn't.»\n- «needn't» + verbo: no hace falta (presente): «You needn't come to the interviews.»\n- «would rather» + verbo: preferir: «I'd rather be there.»\n- «would rather» + otro sujeto + pasado: preferir que otro…: «I'd rather we hired a designer.»\n- «had better (not)» + verbo: más vale que…, consejo con advertencia: «We'd better decide soon.»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Estructura",
                        "Significado",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "needn't have + participio",
                          "lo hicimos, pero no hacía falta",
                          "We needn't have advertised."
                        ],
                        [
                          "didn't need to + verbo",
                          "no hacía falta (y normalmente no se hizo)",
                          "We didn't need to advertise, so we didn't."
                        ],
                        [
                          "needn't + verbo",
                          "no hace falta (presente)",
                          "You needn't come to the interviews."
                        ],
                        [
                          "would rather + verbo",
                          "preferir (yo)",
                          "I'd rather be there."
                        ],
                        [
                          "would rather + sujeto + pasado",
                          "preferir que otro…",
                          "I'd rather we hired a designer first."
                        ],
                        [
                          "had better (not) + verbo",
                          "más vale que…",
                          "We'd better decide soon."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "We needn't have advertised. Helen sent us three excellent CVs.",
                      "I'd rather we hired a designer first.",
                      "We'd better not waste any time.",
                      "I'd rather be there. It's our first hire."
                    ]
                  }
                },
